**Text:** Thanks for updating the spreadsheet. I can tell you put a lot of care into it.

**Listen for:** Plain should sound sincere. Directed should mean the opposite of the words. Nothing in the text marks the sarcasm, so only direction can carry it.

**Directed, as prose:** Dry, cutting sarcasm. The speaker is annoyed and means the opposite of every word. Lean on 'a lot of care'
