### C · Code-switching on look-alike words

{% sample title="Clip C · Code-switching on look-alike words" %}
**Text:** When I asked about the train, she said "son las once," so we'd missed it. My uncle just shrugged: "also gut."

**Listen for:** "son las once" as Spanish and "also gut" as German, though both are spelled like English words.

**Roughly how it sounds:** son lahs OHN-seh ("it's eleven o'clock"); AHL-zo goot ("well, fine").

**Directed, as prose:** Speak in natural American English, but say the quoted Spanish and German phrases in those languages.
{% /sample %}

