### W · Water boiling

{% sample title="Clip W · Water boiling" %}
**Text:** Water boils at 100 °C at sea level, but at 3,000 m (about twice the height of Denver) it boils at about 90, which is why pasta takes longer up there.

**Listen for:** The units read as words (degrees Celsius, meters), the aside in parentheses set off, and the contrast between sea level and altitude.

**Directed, as prose:** Explain it like a patient teacher, so the contrast between sea level and altitude is clear.
{% /sample %}

