### X · Word stress

{% sample title="Clip X · Word stress" %}
**Text:** I didn't say she stole the money.

**Listen for:** The marked word stressed, and only that one. Stress on "she" means someone else stole it; stress on "money" means she stole something else. Plain is the baseline.

**Stress on “she”, directed, as prose:** Stress the word 'she'; it carries the meaning of the sentence.

**Stress on “money”, directed, as prose:** Stress the word 'money'; it carries the meaning of the sentence.

**Markdown \*she\*:** `I didn't say *she* stole the money.`
{% /sample %}

